# Gwyddion Python Processing Tools

This repository contains a lightweight processing pipeline for working with
Gwyddion surface data. The tooling focuses on three key areas:

* Precise ordering of alignment, scaling, and scar removal operations.
* Export of two-dimensional Power Spectral Density Function (PSDF) artefacts,
  including the angular spectrum statistics.
* Video generation with optional frame stabilisation controlled through a
  single displacement percentage parameter.

## Installation

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Command Line Usage

```bash
python -m gwyddion_pipeline path/to/surface.npy \
  --remove-scars \
  --scale 1.5 \
  --psdf --angular-spectrum \
  --frames frame1.png frame2.png frame3.png \
  --stabilize --max-displacement 7.5
```

The command above processes the provided surface, generates PSDF artefacts, and
exports a stabilised video using the supplied image sequence. The
``--max-displacement`` argument is the only required stabilisation parameter and
represents the maximum expected motion between frames as a percentage of the
frame width.

All artefacts are written to the ``outputs`` directory by default.

### Graphical interface availability

The tooling provided in this repository is currently limited to the Python
command line interface exposed through ``python -m gwyddion_pipeline``. A
graphical user interface is not included at this stage; any GUI-based
manipulation should continue to be performed within the Gwyddion desktop
application itself.
